{"availability":"available","full":"tw0po1nt/FsHttp.Studio","name":"FsHttp.Studio","description":"A VSCode extension that runs FsHttp requests from your F# scripts and renders the response richly - images, JSON, HTML, and more","category":"Developer tools","language":"F#","stars":15,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-15T19:45:40Z","updated":"2026-10-11T02:55:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["dotnet","fable","fsharp","fshttp","http-client","rest-client","vscode-extension"],"demo":"https://pokeapi.co/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:36.986Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:36.986Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:36.986Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T07:26:36.986Z","stars":15,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A VSCode extension that runs a single FsHttp request from your F# script and renders the response (images, JSON, HTML) instead of flattening it to text.","FsHttp is a code-first replacement for Postman and .http files, and it uses FSI as the driver. But FSI can only print. It flattens every response into a string:","Seeing the response is the part that makes a request tool worth using, and it is the exact part FSI cannot do. FSI's printer also destroys the response body, because that body is read-once by default. Reading the bytes yourself is therefore a trap."],"features":["an image becomes a byte dump,","a JSON payload becomes one dense line you cannot browse,","an HTML page becomes escaped source."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/tw0po1nt/FsHttp.Studio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"465dbc875d887c4af613099393e224e6d9b75bbe3fdb49511467928fe15792f8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:21.122Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T07:26:37.081Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A VSCode extension that runs a single FsHttp request from your F# script and renders the response (images, JSON, HTML) instead of flattening it to text.",